## Required Remediation Before Re-review

1. Replace recursive projection graph traversal with a bounded iterative
   implementation, and add a post-mutation projection test at the exact accepted
   depth boundary plus one-over rejection.
2. Implement the locked D20 `clickedScene` and `allScenes` semantics, including
   complete all-scene snapshot/restore and shared-occurrence consistency; replace
   the regression that currently expects rejection.
3. Implement R09 Split/Merge around the selected node/mesh/material sharing
   graph, preserve stable IDs through the real operation, check equivalence, and
   test node references, materials, orphan deletion, primitive order, reload,
   no-candidate no-op, and cross-document failure.
4. Add schema-aware validation for every locked material extension and run
   min/mid/max/add/remove/save/reload cases; generic JSON validity is not enough.
5. Replace or supplement the random loop with a replayable independent semantic
   oracle that checks every scene hierarchy, revision/result semantics, a fresh
   projection, complete runtime mapping, and all typed IDs after every operation,
   across the complete P3 mutation surface.

